## Background

The current [RecipeManager.tsx](file:///c:/Users/Rangga Saputra/Documents/Pro_Trial/frontend/src/components/RecipeManager.tsx) already implements a HUD layout that is **very close** to the Figma design. The existing code has the same structural decomposition (top status bar → progress → three-column body with timers/recipe/utility panels). The task is to refine visuals, colors, spacing, and micro-details to **pixel-match** the Figma.

## Analysis: Current Code vs Figma Delta

After comparing the existing implementation against the Figma data and exported screenshot, the differences are **cosmetic refinements**, not structural rewrites:

| Area | Current State | Figma Target | Delta |
|------|--------------|--------------|-------|
| **Outer container** | `bg-[#030908]`, rounded-[34px], cyan border | `bg-[#0A0F1A]`, rounded-[36px], cyan glow border | Tweak bg color, border-radius, shadow |
| **Inner container** | `bg-[#101727]/88` | `bg-[#0F1626]` + `border: 0.8px rgba(0,184,219,0.2)` + `box-shadow: 0 0 60px rgba(0,200,255,0.13)` | Refine bg, add cyan glow shadow |
| **Status badges** | `rounded-[18px]`, `bg-[#101727]/70` | `rounded-[10px]`, `bg rgba(8,14,22,0.5)` | Tighter radius, darker bg |
| **WebSocket badge** | Green dot `#4DFFB3` ✅ matches | Same | No change needed |
| **Gesture badge** | Purple border `rgba(180,71,255,0.34)` | Same | Matches already |
| **Progress bar** | Gradient from-[#19cce5] to-[#b6fbff] | `linear-gradient(90deg, #00D3F3, #A2F4FD)` | Slightly different gradient stops |
| **Section labels** | `text-[#37c6dc]`, tracking-[0.48em] | `rgba(83,234,253,0.7)`, tracking 30% (~0.3em) | Adjust color + tracking |
| **Timer panel** | `rounded-[26px]` | `rounded-[24px]` | Minor radius tweak |
| **Circular timer rings** | SVG circles with strokeWidth 5/3/8 | Figma shows concentric rings with dashed inner ring + thicker outer stroke + glow effects | Refine ring structure, add glow shadows |
